WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:29.980
We'll be right back.

00:30.000 --> 00:59.980
We'll be right back.

01:00.000 --> 01:01.600
So I think we've got to talk about that.

01:01.760 --> 01:05.180
There has apparently been some hacks of some cold wallets or some sort of exploit.

01:05.660 --> 01:07.900
There's also other types of scammery to look out for.

01:08.140 --> 01:12.420
And other than that, I think hopefully if we can close this week bullish, then it's on.

01:12.600 --> 01:15.440
We've got some new cycles in place and new trades can be placed.

01:15.540 --> 01:20.640
I've started to be placed already and hopefully we can get a bit more exposure on at long last.

01:20.780 --> 01:22.140
So let's dig into today.

01:22.140 --> 01:29.340
So first of all, there has apparently been some very, very convincing fake IRS letters being sent out.

01:29.460 --> 01:30.640
So watch out for those.

01:30.760 --> 01:35.640
OK, the second thing is apparently there's been some partial Bitcoin wallet thefts.

01:35.740 --> 01:38.220
And the root cause, I think, is still unclear at the moment.

01:38.220 --> 01:54.620
If you have Bitcoin residing under a single key that was generated on a cold card, I think it's Mark 2 and Mark 3, by the way, between these two dates, 21 and 2023, and you didn't incorporate dice rolls, you didn't use a passphrase and you did not use multi-sig, you should probably move the funds as soon as possible.

01:54.620 --> 01:58.320
So it's a weird time to say this, but you should get your coins onto exchanges.

02:01.080 --> 02:02.920
Seriously, though, do be safe out there, OK?

02:03.440 --> 02:13.060
And I do wonder, you know, if this starts to get worse and worse into the upcoming cycle low, could it be the narrative that the market and aggregate grabs to explain away the cycle price action?

02:13.360 --> 02:14.280
We're going to find out soon enough.

02:14.640 --> 02:19.820
In other news, PCE came out yesterday, and I believe this is probably the last kind of thing we needed to get out of the way.

02:19.880 --> 02:22.720
We got FOMC and, of course, remained paused as expected.

02:22.720 --> 02:25.420
And now we've seen colder PCE prints.

02:25.540 --> 02:29.680
So, again, very much expected, if you've been watching this channel, did have weaker GDP.

02:30.160 --> 02:32.960
But at the end of the day, OK, most of the uncertainty has been removed.

02:33.360 --> 02:39.780
The people that were speculating on sticky inflation and rate hikes and that kind of jazz, again, are hard invalidated.

02:39.940 --> 02:44.980
And now that they can be forced to accept they're hard invalidated, they can move on and start buying things again.

02:44.980 --> 02:54.080
It's also pretty interesting that I didn't even know about this guy, but Leopold got liquidated after facing a huge margin call on various AI-connected positions.

02:54.460 --> 02:57.960
And now the NASDAQ has liquidated its position and its fund, right?

02:58.060 --> 03:00.000
Now it can start to bounce and print its cycle low.

03:00.080 --> 03:06.640
So it is weird how often the market and these cycles act as heat-seeking missiles for over-leveraged players.

03:06.820 --> 03:07.900
And you can see that here, right?

03:07.940 --> 03:11.080
So far, we've got this huge bullish engulfing candle in the NASDAQ.

03:11.080 --> 03:15.420
OK, we've had the fake breakdowns, we have had the quick wicks through the big moving averages,

03:15.420 --> 03:20.220
and we're in the process of finding that swing and confirming it with all the confirmation signals.

03:20.320 --> 03:21.540
We'll get to the charts in just a moment.

03:21.860 --> 03:25.720
But if there was a case for a bottom to be in and a new cycle to be upon us,

03:25.720 --> 03:29.180
I think this is the strongest candidate we've had in the last three weeks.

03:29.520 --> 03:30.700
I found this from Henrik this morning.

03:30.780 --> 03:31.580
I wanted to point this out.

03:31.620 --> 03:32.300
It's pretty interesting.

03:32.480 --> 03:37.660
OK, this right here was a big breakout in the 30-year government yield in June 2007.

03:37.660 --> 03:42.460
Notice how you get the breakout, the hard retest, type 3, where it comes back below the breakout level.

03:42.780 --> 03:47.960
OK, and then we print a marginal higher high on bearish RSI divergence.

03:48.380 --> 03:52.840
This was, of course, back here, where we then ended up trending down for many years to come.

03:53.140 --> 03:55.040
And at the hard right edge, we have got yet another breakout.

03:55.460 --> 04:01.700
We have also got a marginal higher high pending, perhaps, and massive RSI bearish divergence here.

04:02.080 --> 04:05.000
Henrik thinks that the rates are soon going to be going to the downside.

04:05.000 --> 04:07.260
I think so, too, to be completely honest with you.

04:07.360 --> 04:09.500
And again, you've probably heard me say this a million times over.

04:09.600 --> 04:12.260
I still maintain this is one of the most contrarian calls out there at the moment,

04:12.260 --> 04:16.660
because it's really only a handful of people that are pretty steadfast in this position.

04:17.000 --> 04:19.280
There's Henrik, there's David Hunter, and there's me.

04:19.400 --> 04:21.820
And I really don't know anyone else calling for lower rates.

04:21.900 --> 04:24.220
I'm sure, you know, obviously we're not the only three.

04:24.320 --> 04:25.420
I'm sure there'll be some other people.

04:25.580 --> 04:31.280
But generally speaking, out of all the calls and predictions I make and all of the trade setups and everything else,

04:31.280 --> 04:33.980
the only one that people love to poke fun at is this one.

04:33.980 --> 04:35.660
And I do think that's a massive tell here.

04:35.980 --> 04:40.080
Time will tell as always, but you cannot deny that this is really just a bigger one of these.

04:40.400 --> 04:41.480
So we'll see what happens.

04:41.900 --> 04:46.080
And Bitcoin continues to be about most likely to roll over into a daily cycle low.

04:46.140 --> 04:50.120
I'll show you that in just a moment and then probably start to continue to seek out a four-year cycle low

04:50.120 --> 04:52.080
and a weekly cycle low towards the end of this year.

04:52.460 --> 04:55.100
The next big drop likely takes us just below 50k.

04:55.240 --> 04:56.600
So interesting times.

04:56.920 --> 04:58.540
I'll come back and do the stocks last today.

04:58.540 --> 04:59.540
Okay, look at this.

04:59.740 --> 05:03.960
Still absent of clearing the very first hurdle, which means this is left translated and failed,

05:04.060 --> 05:09.540
which means the upcoming daily cycle low, which is due any day now really, should be below both of these lows.

05:09.900 --> 05:16.080
Again, I am interested to see how the people that are obsessed with calling a bottom here are going to explain away new lows.

05:16.540 --> 05:17.280
Interesting times.

05:17.400 --> 05:20.520
But as of right now, okay, hard to say that the cycles are not in control here.

05:20.520 --> 05:26.260
And it's funny that even though the stocks are continuing to push higher, Bitcoin is just completely decoupled, right?

05:26.320 --> 05:27.220
It's just, it doesn't care.

05:27.340 --> 05:31.140
It's doing its own four-year cycle and it really doesn't care about anything else, which is cool to see.

05:31.520 --> 05:34.700
Whilst we're here, pretty much the same things apply for these altcoins as well.

05:34.980 --> 05:37.120
Okay, I expect I've drawn a little yellow squiggle here.

05:37.220 --> 05:41.740
I can't remember when I was drawing this, but something like this I think makes sense for Eve come down and sweep this.

05:41.780 --> 05:46.660
And I see a lot of people very, very sure of themselves that people calling for this are wrong.

05:46.660 --> 05:53.100
So again, it could be, but it would fit from a cycle perspective more than just saying this is what comes next.

05:53.260 --> 05:54.260
Again, time will tell.

05:54.680 --> 05:58.440
For the precious metals, these are still behaving very nicely for us, aren't they?

05:58.580 --> 05:59.760
Okay, no real changes.

05:59.940 --> 06:04.040
We didn't expect anything material to happen until we get to about that mid-September timeframe.

06:04.240 --> 06:08.680
I think it's about the 21st if it was perfect, but obviously give it a bit of wiggle room as always.

06:09.000 --> 06:11.840
But gold and silver and the miners are continuing to set up.

06:12.120 --> 06:15.440
It looks to me like we're probably going to get something more like this and then a spill.

06:15.440 --> 06:19.240
All right, I reckon that's how it's going to go, but there's one of a few paths it could take.

06:19.380 --> 06:20.860
Ultimately, we don't really care about the path.

06:20.940 --> 06:24.340
We care about getting a high probability low to structure and manage the trades around.

06:24.660 --> 06:26.920
And I still maintain that it's just a little bit early.

06:27.100 --> 06:28.440
All right, it's a little bit early here.

06:28.840 --> 06:33.840
I actually think possibly we're going to get on the weekly timeframe some sort of divergence build here.

06:33.900 --> 06:38.360
Like we might get a fake cross and then an uncross and then one higher high on the oscillator here.

06:38.500 --> 06:40.280
Or excuse me, a higher low on the oscillator here.

06:40.540 --> 06:44.040
So this will kind of look like this, like bullish cross, quickly uncrosses, higher low,

06:44.040 --> 06:45.280
and then it will sweep.

06:45.400 --> 06:49.700
And I think that will correspond to something approximating this and a spill.

06:49.920 --> 06:51.840
And that's where you get the divergence, right?

06:51.920 --> 06:55.840
So you get the higher low come in here in line with the lower low in the price.

06:55.840 --> 06:56.700
And then I think it's on.

06:57.100 --> 06:57.820
So we'll see.

06:57.920 --> 07:00.480
As ever, a bit more time is going to go a long way here,

07:00.480 --> 07:02.600
but we're very close to setting this up now, aren't we?

07:02.640 --> 07:03.480
So that's happy days.

07:03.840 --> 07:06.520
Oil continues to do what it was expected to do for now.

07:06.660 --> 07:10.180
I still see a bunch of people that really think $200 a barrel is coming,

07:10.180 --> 07:11.720
but there's your lower high, okay?

07:11.840 --> 07:15.140
And this time, underside retest of the fake breakout level.

07:15.380 --> 07:17.960
So something like this probably does come next, I would think.

07:18.240 --> 07:21.160
And of course, we're still seeking the major yearly low down here.

07:21.440 --> 07:25.100
Given the FOMC and the PCE data are out the way,

07:25.160 --> 07:29.100
you can see the VIX spike is now hopefully going to get crushed into VIX Crush Friday.

07:29.520 --> 07:32.360
And that should be conducive to some pushes here.

07:32.480 --> 07:33.180
This is the Dow.

07:33.300 --> 07:36.400
I would expect the Russell is probably going to break out and confirm today.

07:36.400 --> 07:38.720
Okay, so that would be another trade setup idea there.

07:38.860 --> 07:43.980
I would think the likes of the semiconductors are going to be getting ready here.

07:44.100 --> 07:46.820
I would think the likes of the semiconductors are going to be breaking out

07:46.820 --> 07:48.120
and confirming this is the low today.

07:48.240 --> 07:50.300
I wonder if the indicator is ready to pick this yet.

07:50.500 --> 07:51.900
Probably wants to see the open first.

07:52.160 --> 07:54.920
Yeah, so you see how it's trained to wait for a nice setup here

07:54.920 --> 07:56.380
and it's waited and patiently waited.

07:56.460 --> 07:58.980
And now we're going to get ready to pick this low as it breaks out and confirms.

07:59.300 --> 08:02.880
And then I would think you've got pretty good R&R trade here as well for the semis.

08:03.240 --> 08:05.520
Something approximating this.

08:05.520 --> 08:07.780
Yes, at least four to one here, I would think.

08:08.160 --> 08:10.860
The Nasdaq up three and a bit percent as of yesterday.

08:11.020 --> 08:12.180
That is clearly a swing.

08:12.600 --> 08:14.360
Probably slightly early to be picking this.

08:14.420 --> 08:15.720
I wonder if the indicator thinks it's in.

08:15.780 --> 08:18.300
No, but we're at the edge of the window based on the last cycle low,

08:18.400 --> 08:19.440
getting ready to cross bullish.

08:19.860 --> 08:22.620
So again, if today can open and close strong,

08:22.780 --> 08:24.040
which it looks like it's going to.

08:24.200 --> 08:24.900
Okay, here we go.

08:24.980 --> 08:26.620
On the US 100, that's it.

08:26.680 --> 08:27.040
We're in.

08:27.260 --> 08:28.180
We're above the 10 SMA.

08:28.260 --> 08:28.920
We've got a confirmation.

08:29.600 --> 08:30.660
So there you go.

08:31.240 --> 08:32.400
Patience has gone a long way.

08:32.400 --> 08:36.740
I would now say that we are late enough to the trade to be confident that we are going

08:36.740 --> 08:39.080
to have a good push here and the probabilities are in our favor.

08:39.240 --> 08:42.640
I would now say that something approximating this is probably coming next.

08:42.860 --> 08:43.020
All right.

08:43.040 --> 08:45.000
I don't think that's too insane.

08:45.360 --> 08:45.540
Yeah.

08:45.700 --> 08:45.980
Yeah.

08:46.100 --> 08:46.660
How good is that?

08:46.880 --> 08:49.240
So I think something like this could easily be coming next.

08:49.500 --> 08:51.900
And of course, as ever, we just want to take it one day at a time,

08:51.960 --> 08:56.120
build that exposure up slowly and be open this time to left translation and failure in here.

08:56.440 --> 08:57.540
Hence having a short queued.

08:57.540 --> 09:01.500
Because if we can't smash straight through to new highs, then we will left translate and fail.

09:01.580 --> 09:04.940
And if we do that, then we want to be short into here, which is the exact same setup

09:04.940 --> 09:07.020
as this Bitcoin short right here.

09:07.180 --> 09:10.920
So, I mean, I've been saying the same stuff every day for about three weeks now.

09:11.260 --> 09:12.940
Hopefully you have found some value here.

09:13.020 --> 09:16.700
Hopefully there's some actionable setups for you to manage your risk around some high probability

09:16.700 --> 09:17.240
lows there.

09:17.360 --> 09:20.420
Of course, if you're a level three member, I'll notify you with the exact levels for entry

09:20.420 --> 09:21.860
and stop loss in real time.

09:21.860 --> 09:26.120
As I continue to add more trades, I'm probably going to add one before the open and probably one

09:26.120 --> 09:28.780
after the open in the New York session today.

09:29.160 --> 09:30.820
And then all we really need is some green closes.

09:30.940 --> 09:34.260
And I think we can kind of put our feet up and say, okay, we did our job.

09:34.380 --> 09:35.620
We found the high probability setup.

09:35.740 --> 09:36.940
We managed the risk around the lows.

09:37.020 --> 09:39.040
And now it's just a case of seeing what the market will give.

09:39.180 --> 09:39.320
Okay.

09:39.340 --> 09:41.620
And if it's going to give new highs, then we're here for it.

09:41.860 --> 09:45.200
And if it's going to give that lower high left translation and failure, then it's time

09:45.200 --> 09:45.780
to flip short.

09:46.140 --> 09:47.980
So nice, simple if then conditions.

09:48.160 --> 09:51.160
Now it's really just the case of not getting in the way of ourselves, right?

09:51.160 --> 09:55.000
Be disciplined, have a plan, trade the plan, and most importantly, keep the risk managed.

09:55.000 --> 09:55.840
I'm your boy, Camel.

09:55.880 --> 09:57.200
Have a fantastic weekend.

09:57.380 --> 09:57.920
All the best from me.

09:57.960 --> 09:58.260
Take care.

09:58.380 --> 09:58.580
Cheers.

09:58.700 --> 09:58.840
Bye.

